course: dictionary
lesson: 13910
title: The former and the latter
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Latter means the second of two things or people you have just named. Think of it as "the one mentioned last" when there are only two. «Tea or coffee? I'll have the latter.» Only two drinks were offered, and the second one, coffee, is the latter.
explain: Writers use this word to avoid repeating names. «Mia and Sam both wanted the red bike. The former asked first, but the latter got it.» The former is the first of two, so Mia asked first. The latter is the second of two, so Sam got the bike. To find the meaning, go back to the two names just mentioned.
explain: Latter also means near the end of a time. «The latter part of the film was very sad.» Here latter does not point back to two things. It tells you which part: the end, after the middle. Clue words like part, half and years help you spot this meaning.
fact: Latter means the second of two things just mentioned.
fact: The former means the first of two, and the latter means the second of two.
fact: Use latter for two things only. For three or more, use last or final.
fact: «The latter half of the book» means the second half, near the end.
fact: A quick check: find the two things just named, then pick the one named second.
exercise: «Cat or dog? I chose the latter.» Which did I choose? | Both | Neither | Cat | *Dog
exercise: «Ravi and Pete ran the race. The former came first, and the latter came second.» Who came second? | Ravi | Neither ran | *Pete | Both came first
exercise: Which phrase means near the end of a time? | The front row | *The latter half | The first hour | The former half
test: «Apples or pears? She picked the latter.» What did she pick? | Apples | Both | *Pears | Neither
test: «The latter years of his life were quiet.» What does latter mean here? | The first years | Happy years | Years with the family | *The last years, near the end
exam: «Ben and Lily came in. The former sat down, and the latter stood.» Who stood? | Ben | *Lily | Both | Neither
